# Copy to .env.local. Never commit the copy.

# WalletConnect project id. Without one, @gullylabs/core-connect omits every
# WalletConnect-backed wallet from the modal rather than offering rows that
# cannot complete a connection.
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# A dedicated RPC endpoint, used ahead of the SDK's probed public list.
# A keyed provider embeds its credential in the URL path, which is why this is
# an env var and not a line in gullycore.config.ts.
VITE_RPC_URL=

# An API key with the `router:quote` scope for Gully Core's routing API (or your
# own), read by gullycore.config.ts `routing.apiKey`. Anonymous quotes work
# without one, rate-limited per address. Never commit a key.
#
# Get one at https://gullychain.xyz/core/developers: sign in with a wallet, up to 3
# keys per wallet, scopes public:read + router:quote, the secret shown once.
#
# A VITE_ variable is COMPILED INTO THE PUBLIC BUNDLE: anyone who loads your
# site can read this key and spend its rate limit. It cannot move funds (its
# scopes are read and quote), and you can revoke it at /developers. Leave it
# empty unless the anonymous limit is what is stopping you, or put it on a
# server of your own that forwards quotes (the SDK's router client sends it as
# X-API-Key and is written to run server side).
VITE_GULLYCORE_ROUTER_KEY=
